CommitDate: Sun Sep 27 17:44:25 2026 -0500

    feat(play): MCP tool surface for the live game + pause/saves/reset
    
    The game is now tools, not shell commands. scripts/aipp_mcp.py is an MCP stdio
    server exposing 12 tools: game_observe, game_screenshot (returns a real IMAGE
    block, not a path to read), game_press, game_step, game_pause, game_resume,
    game_save, game_load, game_list_saves, game_delete_save, game_reset (cold-boot to
    the title screen) and game_health.
    
    Verified: initialize -> aipp-game 1.0.0, tools/list -> 12 tools, and tools/call
    game_health returned live bridge data over the stdio handshake.
    
    The bridge grew the matching commands (pause/resume/list_saves/delete_save/reset)
    and a settle flag. Pause is enforced, not decorative: with the game paused a press
    returns "paused - call resume first" and does not move the player. Saves are
    listable and deletable (verified: slot_probe written then deleted).
    
    Registered with Hermes as mcp_servers.aipp-game pointing at
    scripts/aipp-mcp-wrapper.sh, which resolves the per-session token in one place and
    fails closed when it is absent.
    
    NOTE, verified rather than assumed: a newly registered MCP server is NOT hot-loaded
    into a running session. tool_search in the live session does not list aipp-game
    among its sources; the catalog is built at session start. It becomes available to
    sessions started after the next MCP reload.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
